Two-Headed Giant (Commander Duels v0.5.0 spike), part 1 of 2: shared team turns (rule 805).

Reason: XMage has no team game. This lets a game type name each player's teammates
(Game.getTeammates, empty by default, so every other game type is unchanged) and makes the core
rules use them: the active team takes one turn together (805.4: the next player in turn order skips
the turn their teammate just took; every player on the team untaps, draws, may play a land and
discards to hand size; 805.9: each of them is an active player, for sorcery timing, "your turn" and
"at the beginning of your upkeep"), teammates are not opponents, the active team declares its
attackers together (805.10b) and the defending team blocks together (805.10d). XMage's human player
treats the team's turn as its own when choosing where to stop. Commander Duels' TwoHeadedGiant game
type (engine/src/main/java/com/commanderduels/TwoHeadedGiant.java) supplies the teams.
Upstream: none yet; to be offered to magefree/mage once the format is proven.
Remove when: XMage upstream implements shared team turns, or Two-Headed Giant is dropped.

